      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We need to find ${n \\choose k}$.\nTo compute the binomial coefficient ${n \\choose k}$, we plug in the given values of $n = 6$ and $k = 4$ into ${n \\choose k} = \\dfrac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$.\nThis gives us ${6 \\choose 4} = \\dfrac{6!}{4!(10)!}$.\nSimplifying the factorial expressions, we have ${6 \\choose 4} = \\dfrac{6 \\times 5}{2 \\times 1} = \\boxed{15}$.\nThe answer is: 15",
